A||||24||Joe Torma||3400 G-Tech results...kinda||||1||
Z||000000||Joe Torma||10-21-2001||09:53 PM||||Well, once again, I steath-ally took my Fiero out tonight...<P>0-60 in 5.98 seconds with 2 problems.<P>First off the darn car doesn't hook up anymore.  It will spin through 1st and second.  When cruising along in second, it will spin them on demand @ whatever speed when I slam the hammer down.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Got any suggestions?<P>And it took me AT LEAST ONE SECOND to get the frickin thing in second gear.  Something needs adjustment.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I couldn't datalog the event cause it threw my laptop all around and knocked the battery out...it was kinda secure?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Oh well, I'll tinker with the shifter and see what I can do tomorrow.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||10-21-2001||10:15 PM||||Dude, are you running the 3400SFI that comes in the new Grand Ams?  How hard was it to mount?  I've got a 99 Grand Am with the 3400SFI, and it is indeed a sweet engine.  Hmmm, maybe I should swap it for the 2.8 in my Formula?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||10-21-2001||10:40 PM||||Yup that's the one...but mine is out of a minivan.  It wasn't that bad to install.  It needed a new front mount, and a scoop/vent in the lid.<P>They now make a supercharger for the Grand Am.  I'm trying to see if it'll fit...but the Grand Am forum people aren't being too helpful.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||10-21-2001||11:08 PM|||| O-sh*t I’m in trouble! I'm going to have to do some more modifications to keep up with that. (jk)<P>Very cool! Sounds like you have some impressive torque. How is the high end horsepower? Does it pull to 6k rpm? What did you get for a quarter mile reading and rear wheel horsepower?<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rmorgandotcom||10-21-2001||11:13 PM||||Spins on command, wow, that sounds powerful.<BR>I think its creepy that there is a 88formula and a Formula88.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rmorgansig.jpg">   <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE> <BR><LI><I><FONT COLOR="blue">project - finale body on a 86 4 cylinder 5 speed</FONT></I><BR><LI><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/</A><BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||10-21-2001||11:19 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Yup that's the one...but mine is out of a minivan.  It wasn't that bad to install.  It needed a new front mount, and a scoop/vent in the lid.<P>They now make a supercharger for the Grand Am.  I'm trying to see if it'll fit...but the Grand Am forum people aren't being too helpful.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cool!  Which forum?  I'm on <A HREF="http://www.grandamgt.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grandamgt.com</A>  and they seem pretty cool.  I don't think they'll be much help in the swap aspects, but lots of info on mods and such.  Most of the people on there want to just buy a bolt on out of the box, rather than do fab work that Fiero people do all the time.  They've got a few people running the supercharger on their 3400.  It's supposed to up the output to about 260HP, so it's slightly stronger than the 3800SC.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||1
